{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789853007,"nonce":"XXeeszJY5Tq2mupClXjc/avjhAY=","title":"Hot reload matched an edited body's resume points on full site keys, which its body tag never lets match","message":"Since 47fe421 an OSR site key carries a body tag in its top 16 bits, so a resume point made for one body is entered only by frames running that body. A reload compiles the edited body's helpers and matched their sites against the running code's with the full key: the tags differ by construction, every helper fell back (\"site 0x...: running code has no such loop\"), the running loop finished on the old code and a suspended fiber never migrated. zynml hot_reload_loop_boundary::a_running_loop_finishes_in_the_edited_code and hot_reload_fibers::a_suspended_fiber_keeps_its_state_and_picks_up_the_edit failed.\n\nThe reload now matches on the tag-less part of the key (osr::site_loop: loop ordinal and live-in count) with the same layout check as before, and publishes the helper under the running code's key, which its probes carry.","files":null}]}